## Finding

D requires generated views to carry a full root and a lens of the deciding code path, its parameters, trust, profile and pins. At M, all three public commands `python3 -m warrant.roadmap view`, `python3 -m warrant.claims view`, and `python3 -m warrant.review view` successfully generate Markdown with only a 12-character snapshot prefix and no lens. The first two also print only a 12-character assessment prefix. These are public CLI outputs, not just unwrapped internal helper returns; each command also exposes `--out`.

The wrapper `tools/graph.py render` adds a full root/lens at lines 66-70, but these public commands do not call it. Thus fixing that wrapper did not finish the generated-view part of D. Consumers of these outputs cannot identify the full store state and deciding lens from the view itself. This finding does not assert a new collision in the wrapped views.

